  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Npc191948 and CCF-STTG1, mediated through the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including (1R,3R,4S,7S,9S,11S,13R,14R,15R)-4,11,13,14-tetrahydroxy-7-[(2Z,4R)-4-(hydroxymethyl)hex-2-en-2-yl]-3,9,15-trimethoxy-12,12-dimethyl-6,17-dioxabicyclo[11.3.1]heptadecan-5-one, 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol, and (+)-(5S,7R)-7-Ethoxy-12-Hydroxy-2-Oxo-20-Norabieta-1(10),8,11,13-Tetraene. These compounds are all implicated in the regulation of the 26S proteasome, which is a key component in the ubiquitin-proteasome system. The final scores for these relationships are relatively high, indicating a plausible biological connection. The evidence suggests that Npc191948 may interact with CCF-STTG1 through the 26S proteasome, potentially modulating its activity. However, the exact mechanism of interaction and the role of these compounds in the biological process remain to be fully elucidated.",
